[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:43. Fully Insured]
[00:00.741] Passage 43. | 第43篇文章。
[00:02.635] Fully insured. | 全额投保。
[00:05.300] Insurance companies are normally willing to insure anything. | 保险公司通常愿意为任何事物投保。
[00:09.405] Insuring public or private property is a standard practice in most countries around the world. | 为公共或私人财产投保是世界上大多数国家的标准做法。
[00:14.760] If, however, you were holding an open-air garden party or a fate, | 然而，如果你正在举办一场露天花园派对或游园会，
[00:18.800] it would be equally possible to insure yourself in the event of bad weather. | 那么为应对恶劣天气而投保也同样是可能的。
[00:23.025] Needless to say, the bigger the risk an insurance company takes, | 不用说，保险公司承担的风险越大，
[00:26.750] the higher the premium you will have to pay. | 你需要支付的保费就越高。
[00:29.615] It is not uncommon to hear that a shipping company | 经常听说一家航运公司
[00:32.690] has made a claim for the lost ship. | 为失事船只提出了索赔。
[00:35.350] But the claim made by a local authority | 但是，地方当局提出的索赔
[00:38.555] to recover the cost of salvaging a sunken pie dish | 为了收回打捞一个沉没的馅饼盘的成本
[00:42.775] must surely be unique. | 肯定是非同寻常的。
[00:45.290] Admittedly, it was an unusual pie dish, | 诚然，那是一个不同寻常的馅饼盘，
[00:48.975] for it was 18 feet long and 6 feet wide. | 因为它有18英尺长，6英尺宽。
[00:52.470] It had been purchased by a local authority | 它是由当地政府购买的，
[00:54.870] so that an enormous pie could be baked for an annual fair. | 以便为一个年度展览烤制一个巨大的馅饼。
[00:58.945] The pie committee decided that the best way to transport the dish would be by canal. | 馅饼委员会决定，运输这个盘子的最佳方式是通过运河。
[01:04.695] So they insured it for the trip. | 于是他们为这次行程投了保。
[01:07.365] Shortly after it was launched, | 启动后不久，
[01:10.105] the pie committee went to a local inn to celebrate. | 馅饼委员会去了一家当地的旅馆庆祝。
[01:13.260] At the same time, a number of teenagers climbed onto the dish | 同时，一些青少年爬上了馅饼盘，
[01:17.915] and held a little party of their own. | 并举办了一个他们自己的小型派对。
[01:20.600] Modern dances proved to be more than the dish could bear, | 现代舞对馅饼盘来说是难以承受的，
[01:24.435] for during the party it capsized | 因为在派对期间它翻覆了，
[01:26.975] and sank in seven feet of water. | 沉入了七英尺深的水中。
[01:30.240] The pie committee telephoned a local garage owner | 馅饼委员会给当地的一位车库老板打了电话，
[01:34.055] who arrived in a recovery truck to salvage the pie dish. | 他开着一辆救援卡车赶来打捞这个馅饼盘。
[01:37.950] Shivering in their wet clothes, | 青少年们穿着湿衣服瑟瑟发抖，
[01:40.085] the teenagers looked on while three men dived repeatedly into the water to locate the dish. | 看着三名男子反复潜入水中寻找馅饼盘。
[01:46.390] They had little difficulty in finding it, | 他们很快就找到了它，
[01:49.045] but hauling it out of the water | 但是把它从水里拖出来
[01:51.295] proved to be a serious problem. | 却是个大问题。
[01:53.965] The sides of the dish were so smooth | 馅饼盘的侧面非常光滑，
[01:56.735] that it was almost impossible to attach ropes and chains to the rim without damaging it. | 几乎不可能在不损坏它的情况下将绳索和链条固定在边缘。
[02:02.125] Eventually, chains were fixed to one end of the dish | 最终，链条被固定在馅饼盘的一端，
[02:06.260] and a powerful winch was put into operation. | 一个强力绞车投入了使用。
[02:09.865] The dish rose to the surface | 馅饼盘浮出水面，
[02:12.055] and was gently drawn towards the canal bank. | 然后被轻轻地拉向运河岸边。
[02:15.395] For one agonizing moment, | 在一个令人痛苦的时刻，
[02:18.045] the dish was perched precariously on the bank of the canal. | 馅饼盘摇摇晃晃地停在运河岸边。
[02:22.510] But it suddenly overbalanced and slipped back into the water. | 但它突然失去平衡，滑回了水中。
[02:26.725] The men were now obliged to try once more. | 这些人现在不得不再次尝试。
[02:30.545] This time, they fixed heavy metal clamps to both sides of the dish | 这次，他们将重型金属夹固定在馅饼盘的两侧，
[02:35.865] so that they could fasten the chains. | 这样他们就可以固定链条了。
[02:38.275] The dish now had to be lifted vertically because one edge was resting against the side of the canal. | 馅饼盘现在必须垂直吊起，因为一侧正抵着运河的侧壁。
[02:44.570] The winch was again put into operation | 绞车再次投入使用，
[02:47.650] and one of the men started up the truck. | 其中一人启动了卡车。
[02:50.395] Several minutes later, | 几分钟后，
[02:52.360] the dish was successfully hauled above the surface of the water. | 馅饼盘被成功地吊出水面。
[02:56.380] Water streamed in torrents over its sides | 水从馅饼盘的两侧倾泻而下，
[02:59.916] with such force that it set up a huge wave in the canal. | 力量之大，以至于在运河中激起了巨大的波浪。
[03:03.930] There was danger that the wave would rebound off the other side of the bank | 危险在于，波浪会从运河的另一边反弹回来，
[03:08.570] and send the dish plunging into the water again. | 再次将馅饼盘冲入水中。
[03:12.030] By working at tremendous speed, | 通过以极快的速度工作，
[03:14.500] the men managed to get the dish onto dry land | 男人们设法在波浪返回之前
[03:17.335] before the wave returned. | 将馅饼盘弄到了岸上。